# Q20: add the independent-line tests of the red ridge to /output/report.json (from s110a-e). Re-runnable: starts from out/report_before_q20.json (first run saves it).
import json,shutil,os
R='/output/report.json'; B='/workspace/out/report_before_q20.json'
if not os.path.exists(B): shutil.copy(R,B)
r=json.load(open(B)); res=[x for x in r['results'] if not x['evidence'].startswith('Q20:')]
A=lambda n,v:{'name':n,'value':v}
com=[A('data','Xb47 (Band 7) HCN 4-3 spw16, HCO+ 4-3 spw18, CS 7-6 spw22, H13CN 4-3 spw20 (native beam 4.1-4.3 x 2.7-2.8", PA 87; 0.53" pixels; dv 3.3-3.4 km/s) and Xb4d (0.94x0.74") 3-2, SO 6_5-5_4 spw31, HC3N 28-27 spw29; all pbcor, VSYS 2780 km/s radio-LSRK'),
 A('beam','1" apertures are impossible in Band 7 (beam 4.1x2.7"; ridge is 1.9" from N and 3.3" from S, 5.2" apart nuclei): all 3-2 and 4-3 comparisons are at one common 4.5x3.0" beam PA 87 (flux rescaled); the 1" ridge numbers of p0017 cannot be reproduced in B7'),
 A('noise per channel (native, off-source, Jy/beam)','HCN 4-3 5.2 mJy, HCO+ 4-3 6.0, CS 7-6 4.6, H13CN 4.3, SO 1.3 (Xb4d), HCN 3-2 1.5, HCO+ 3-2 1.6'),
 A('method','4-3 window map (red 180-320 / blue -320..-180) = a*core(|v|<150) + b + s*T, T = the observed 3-2 wing excess (core-null residual at 1.05", Gaussian taper sigma 1.5" around ridge or lobe) convolved to 4.5x3.0"; s = F(4-3)/F(3-2) of the excess in Jy at matched beam; Tb ratio r43/32 = s/1.778; errors = max(OLS with effective-beam dof, sd of s with the template displaced 4.5-10")'),
 A('baselines','median of line-free channels (-900..-450; HCO+ 4-3 -630..-450 + 450..880; CS 7-6 -840..-450 + 450..720); H13CN 4-3 sits on the CO 3-2 red tail (linear baseline 450..1000, the spw ends at -225 km/s so no mirrored blue window)')]
def add(q,t,v,u,un,conf,ev,extra=()): res.append(dict(quantity=q,target=t,value=v,uncertainty=u,unit=un,assumptions=com+list(extra),confidence=conf,evidence='Q20: '+ev))
add('Is the red ridge (+180..320 km/s, 3.3" N of S) seen in HCN 4-3 and HCO+ 4-3 (Band 7), and with what profile?',
 'ridge vs S blue lobe, HCN and HCO+ 4-3, 4.5x3.0" matched beam, template = 3-2 excess',
 'WEAKLY YES, consistent with the 3-2 feature but only ~3 sigma. Ridge red excess in units of the 3-2 excess (s): HCN 4-3 1.64+-0.73 (2.3 sigma; 1.35+-0.64 with a 2.5" template taper), HCO+ 4-3 3.6+-1.2 (2.9 sigma; 2.9+-1.1); inverse-variance stack 2.14+-0.63 (3.4 sigma) vs 3-2 stack 1.36+-0.35 (same machinery, 3.9 sigma, i.e. the method recovers ~1 by construction within errors). Lobe (blue): HCN 4-3 1.25+-0.41 (3.0 sigma), HCO+ 4-3 1.16+-0.49; stack 1.21+-0.32 (3.8 sigma; 3-2 stack 1.10+-0.15). Mirror controls (blue window with the ridge template, red with the lobe template): HCN -0.7+-0.9 / +0.2+-0.3, HCO+ +0.2+-1.1 / -0.1+-0.5: no wrong-sign signal. 40-km/s bin profile (Jy/beam km/s at 4.5x3", ridge, bins 160-200..320-360): HCN 4-3 +0.08 +0.18 +0.09 +0.11 0.00 (sd ~0.09) vs 3-2 +0.09 +0.11 +0.08 +0.08 +0.08 (sd ~0.05); HCO+ 4-3 -0.03 +0.21 +0.13 +0.25 +0.15 (sd ~0.11) vs 3-2 -0.10 +0.07 +0.11 +0.12 -0.02: the ridge flux starts at ~200 km/s (fraction of the 160-360 flux in 160-200: HCN 0.18+-0.17 (4-3), 0.22+-0.11 (3-2); HCO+ -0.05 (+0.18/-0.29) (4-3), -0.26 (+0.39/-0.62) (3-2)) whereas the lobe has its largest flux at the lowest |v| and falls (HCO+ lobe fraction in 160-200 0.66 (+0.33/-0.20) at 4-3, 0.48+-0.09 at 3-2; centroid |v| 179 (+30/-55) vs 216+-15 at 3-2; ridge centroid 282 (+31/-22) at 4-3 and 284 (+57/-38) at 3-2). So the p0017 shape difference (narrow ridge starting ~200 km/s vs falling lobe wing) is reproduced in sign in HCO+ 4-3 (ridge centroid 282 vs lobe 179, ~2 sigma) and is weaker in HCN (255/240 vs 238/230: not distinguishable). The 4-3 data therefore add an independent-band, independent-array detection of a red ridge at ~3.4 sigma, but not an independent precision measurement.',
 's 0.6-1.2 (35-45%) per line; ~3 sigma significance','dimensionless (s), sigma','low-moderate','s110a_q20_spectra.py (native spectra, noise), s110b_q20_maps.py (matched-beam maps), s110c_q20_templatefit.py (+ arg 2.5), s110e_q20_summary.py -> out/q20/s110a-e.txt/json')
add('Matched-beam ridge-vs-lobe line-ratio pattern: r43/32 (HCN, HCO+) and HCN/HCO+ of the wing excess; does it discriminate S counter-lobe from Bridge streaming?',
 'ridge vs S blue lobe, 4.5x3.0" common beam, J=3-2 and 4-3',
 'NO. Tb ratio r43/32 of the excess (4-3/3-2 Jy ratio / 1.778): HCN ridge 0.72 (+0.51/-0.34), lobe 0.80 (+0.38/-0.29); HCO+ ridge 1.31 (+1.06/-0.54), lobe 0.50 (+0.24/-0.22) (the ridge HCO+ value is formally >1, so it reflects noise/baseline systematics rather than an inverted excitation). Ridge/lobe ratio of r43/32: HCN 0.90 (+0.97/-0.49), HCO+ 2.8 (+3.8/-1.4; P(ridge<lobe)=0.09, ~1.3 sigma in the opposite sense to the cooling-with-radius expectation) - no pattern. HCN/HCO+ of the excess: 3-2 ridge 1.26 (+0.97/-0.52), lobe 0.96 (+0.31/-0.25); 4-3 ridge 0.69 (+0.52/-0.32), lobe 1.55 (+1.30/-0.63): ridge and lobe both ~1 within 1 sigma, far above the core ratio (HCN/HCO+ core 3-2 ~0.5 at the ridge, 0.36 at the lobe) but this is shared by both, so it says the excess gas is HCN-rich relative to the cores in both places (lobe-like), not which origin. Predictions: a counter-lobe of the same outflow should show lobe-like ratios (observed: consistent), Bridge streaming gas would show Bridge-core-like ratios (HCN/HCO+ ~0.5 at 3-2; observed ridge 1.26 +0.97/-0.52, 1.4 sigma above, not rejected). The 4-3 data give no excitation difference at the 40% level. Excitation arguments are in any case not used to decide origin (M18 1-0 flux scale, Q17). Origin remains undecided; S counter-lobe ~55-65% unchanged.',
 'factor 1.5-2.5 on ratio of ratios','dimensionless','low','s110c_q20_templatefit.py (E1), s110e_q20_summary.py -> out/q20/s110e.txt',[A('thermal limit','r43/32<=1 for thermal beam-filling gas')])
add('Independent weak lines at the ridge and lobe: CS 7-6, SO 6_5-5_4, HC3N 28-27 and H13CN 4-3 upper limits',
 'ridge (red 180-320) and lobe (blue -320..-180)',
 'NONE detected; the limits do not test the ridge. Band 7 (4.5x3.0", F relative to the HCN 3-2 excess at the same place, 3 sigma): CS 7-6 ridge s=0.10+-0.95 -> <2.96 (<0.72 Jy/beam km/s), lobe 0.20+-0.34 -> <1.24; core CS 7-6/HCN 3-2 at the pixel is 0.11-0.14, so the limit is 9-26x the core ratio. H13CN 4-3 ridge s=-4.7+-2.5 (negative, baseline/CO-tail systematics, no blue window) -> <7.6 (formal), about 4x the core ratio (core contaminated by CO) and ~70x the expected H13CN/HCN ~0.05-0.1: uninformative; H13CN 3-2 is not covered. 1" resolution (Xb4d, r=1" apertures as p0017, sd of 267 control apertures 0.027-0.036 Jy km/s): SO 6_5-5_4 ridge red -0.023+-0.027 -> 3-sigma UL 0.082 Jy km/s (<0.32 of the HCN 3-2 ridge excess 0.257; lobe blue -0.019 -> <0.089 = <0.27 of 0.325; SO/HCN in the S core is 0.023, so the limit is ~13x the core ratio); HC3N 28-27 ridge +0.022 -> <0.131 (<0.51 of HCN), lobe +0.008 -> <0.117 (<0.36). Stacking does not help (all limits are far above the expected ~1-5% of HCN); detecting SO or CS at a typical 2-5% of HCN would need ~10-25x lower noise (>100x time). HCN 4-3 itself in Xb47 is the only independent line with a signal (previous entry). Native-resolution peak-pixel spectra at S/N/ridge/lobe are in out/q20/s110a_*.csv (HCN 4-3 peaks 34/99/58/22 mJy/beam at S/N/ridge/lobe; CS 7-6 12/23/13/9 mJy/beam; SO 6_5-5_4 peak <2 mJy/beam, rms 1.3).',
 '3-sigma upper limits','Jy km/s, ratio to HCN 3-2 excess','medium (limits), no detection','s110d_q20_so_hc3n_1arcsec.py -> out/q20/s110d.txt; s110c (CS, SO, H13CN at 4.5x3.0"); s110a (spectra)')
cav=r['caveats']
add_cav='Q20: the Band 7 data (4.1x2.7" beam) cannot isolate the ridge from N (1.9") and S (3.3"): the 4-3 ridge signal is extracted by a template fit assuming the 4-3 excess has the spatial shape of the 3-2 excess (an assumption that biases s if the 4-3 emitting region is more extended), with a free core-wing coefficient (negative for HCN 4-3, -0.03, probably continuum/self-absorption at the nuclei, so the nuclear red wing is not modelled physically) and errors of 35-45%; the ~3 sigma significance is formal (effective dof from beam area, shifted-template null). The HCO+ 4-3 ridge excess is above the thermal limit (r43/32 1.3, 1 sigma). CS 7-6, SO, HC3N and H13CN limits are 9-70x above the core line ratios and cannot test the ridge or the origin; H13CN has no mirrored window and sits on the CO 3-2 wing. 1-0 flux scale unverified (Q17) so no r31 argument is used.'
r['caveats']=(cav+[add_cav]) if isinstance(cav,list) else cav+' | '+add_cav
r['results']=res; json.dump(r,open(R,'w'),indent=1); print(len(res))
